  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;begins to move under the action of a time dependent force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>,&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;are the unit vectors along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;axis. The power developed by above force, at the time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>,&nbsp;will be _______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>.&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "100",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math></p><p>Now, we can write from Newton&#39;s second law,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>d</mo><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>d</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math></p><p>Integrating the above,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>d</mo><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Now, power developed by the force is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>At&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, power is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math></p>",
